WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.251
Spark SQL does not erase the SQL ideas we already
learned Filters

00:00:06.396 --> 00:00:12.433
joins grouping windows NULL handling and row grain
still matter What

00:00:12.446 --> 00:00:18.027
changes is the execution environment In PostgreSQL
we usually think

00:00:18.041 --> 00:00:23.620
about one database engine managing tables and
indexes In Spark the work may run

00:00:23.646 --> 00:00:29.501
across many workers and many data partitions That
means a correct query

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:33.580
can still be expensive if it scans too much data or
causes large shuffles
